  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment is complete (config_004: RNA-only, PCA-2000, multiprofile, avgpool → acc 0.591, F1 0.573). The single most important unresolved question is whether the image modality carries useful signal for this task at all, since this determines whether any of the ~35 multimodal configurations are worth pursuing. Question tested: config_012 (image-only, multiprofile, ResNet50, avgpool) holds profile setting and aggregation identical to config_004, so the only change is modality (RNA → Image). This gives a clean unimodal image baseline to compare against the RNA-only result. Why this is the best next step: With only one data point, the highest-uncertainty design decision is modality value. Establishing the image-only baseline before investing in multimodal fusion experiments avoids wasting budget on complex fusion/aggregation configurations if image information is uninformative. It also isolates the modality effect without confounding with encoder, fusion, or aggregation choices."
}

